  "slug": "multimodal-language-27be",
  "summary": "Agents that call retrieval, structure parsing, literature mining, and notebook execution are now being tested on discrete biological analysis tasks.",
  "synthesis": "The shared thread is the LLM as an orchestration layer that delegates to specialized tools and external resources rather than serving as a model of the data itself. Genie-CAT couples retrieval-augmented generation with PDB parsing, electrostatics calculations, and ML-based redox prediction to propose testable hypotheses for metalloprotein mechanisms. The multi-agent system in the gene-set study, built on Llama 3, DeepSeek, and Qwen, mines PubMed abstracts to verify and expand HPO gene sets with literature-supported genes. kai iteratively constructs computational notebooks for single-cell cell type annotation and is described as model-agnostic. What is new relative to protein language model approaches is the explicit reliance on tool invocation and executable analysis steps, with hypotheses grounded in physical calculations, literature evidence, or notebook code. All three items are preprints, so their benchmark and validation claims have not yet been assessed through peer review.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-27"
}
